---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import PageBanner from '../components/PageBanner.astro';
import { MAP_SETS, CLASSIC_MENU, DIFFICULTY, GAME_MODES, WEAPONS, MORE_SETTINGS, CHEATS, shown } from '../data/classic';
import { url } from '../lib';
---

<Base title="Maps & modes" description="The map sets, difficulties, game modes, weapons, settings and cheats of Super Mario Bros. Crossover: REMIX Classic mode.">
  <PageBanner
    title="Maps & modes"
    intro="Pick Classic on the title screen. The Classic menu lists the map sets, the map difficulty and the options."
  />
  <div class="wrap page">
    <section aria-labelledby="sets">
      <h2 id="sets">Map sets</h2>
      <p>Every map set is open from the start. Each one shows <strong>BEATEN</strong> once you've cleared it.</p>
      <div class="grid">
        {
          shown(MAP_SETS).map((m) => (
            <div class="panel">
              <h3>{m.name}</h3>
              <p>{m.text}</p>
            </div>
          ))
        }
      </div>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="menu">
      <h2 id="menu">The Classic menu and options</h2>
      <ul>{shown(CLASSIC_MENU).map((m) => <li>{m.text}</li>)}</ul>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="difficulty">
      <h2 id="difficulty">Map difficulty: Easy, Normal, Hard</h2>
      <ul>{DIFFICULTY.map((d) => <li>{d.text}</li>)}</ul>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="modes">
      <h2 id="modes">Game modes</h2>
      <p>In <strong>Options → Game mode</strong>.</p>
      <dl class="defs">
        {
          GAME_MODES.map((m) => (
            <div>
              <dt>{m.name}</dt>
              <dd>{m.text}</dd>
            </div>
          ))
        }
      </dl>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="rules">
      <h2 id="rules">Classic rules</h2>
      <p>
        <strong>Options → Classic rules</strong> is on by default: the heroes play as in the original, with its power
        states, physics and weapons, a camera that scrolls back left, and areas kept as you left them. Map difficulty, More
        settings, Weapons and Cheats need these rules. The other choice, <strong>Current</strong>, gives the heroes health
        bars and their own upgrades instead; with it every map plays on Normal and cheats are off.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="weapons">
      <h2 id="weapons">Weapons</h2>
      <p>
        <strong>Options → Weapons</strong>, the original's Customize Weapons, picks each hero's power-up weapon. The
        original's choice (listed first) is the default, and <strong>Restore originals</strong> puts every row back.
      </p>
      <div class="table-wrap panel">
        <table>
          <caption class="visually-hidden">Weapon choices for each hero</caption>
          <thead>
            <tr><th scope="col">Hero (power-up)</th><th scope="col">Choices, default first</th></tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            {
              WEAPONS.map((w) => (
                <tr>
                  <td>{w.row}</td>
                  <td>{w.choices}</td>
                </tr>
              ))
            }
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="more">
      <h2 id="more">More settings</h2>
      <p>With Classic rules. Each setting starts at the original's value; <strong>Restore originals</strong> resets them.</p>
      <dl class="defs">
        {
          MORE_SETTINGS.map((m) => (
            <div>
              <dt>{m.name}</dt>
              <dd>{m.text}</dd>
            </div>
          ))
        }
      </dl>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="cheats">
      <h2 id="cheats">Cheats</h2>
      <p>
        The original's cheats, in <strong>Options → Cheats</strong>, all off by default and for Classic rules only. A
        locked cheat shows as <strong>?????</strong>: select it to see its goal. The original's secret code unlocks them all.
      </p>
      <div class="table-wrap panel">
        <table>
          <caption class="visually-hidden">Cheats, what they do and how to unlock them</caption>
          <thead>
            <tr><th scope="col">Cheat</th><th scope="col">What it does</th><th scope="col">How to unlock it</th></tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            {
              shown(CHEATS).map((c) => (
                <tr>
                  <td>{c.name}</td>
                  <td>{c.does}</td>
                  <td>{c.unlock}</td>
                </tr>
              ))
            }
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <p>
        <strong>Level Select</strong> unlocks once you beat every map set on Hard. It appears on the Cheats page and in the
        pause menu: pick a map set, a difficulty, a world and a level.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="music">
      <h2 id="music">Music set</h2>
      <p>
        <strong>Options → Music set</strong>: <strong>Character</strong> (the default, as in the original) plays each
        hero's own music, <strong>Map</strong> plays the Super Mario Bros. music for everyone, and <strong>Random</strong>{' '}
        picks one of the two for each area. All of the music is our own.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="chapter">
      <h2 id="chapter">Chapter 1</h2>
      <p>
        Chapter 1, our story campaign, is on the title screen too, but it is coming soon (planned for version 1.0). Its
        card says so, and any save files you already have are kept.
      </p>
    </section>

    <p>
      More on the heroes: <a href={url('heroes/')}>Heroes</a>. Controls and accessibility:{' '}
      <a href={url('how-to-play/')}>How to play</a>.
    </p>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .page section {
    margin-top: 2.5rem;
  }
  .page h3 {
    margin-top: 0;
    color: var(--gold);
  }
  .defs > div + div {
    margin-top: 0.85rem;
  }
  .defs dt {
    font-weight: 700;
  }
  .defs dd {
    margin: 0.2rem 0 0;
  }
</style>
